# AssimpForUnreal test fixture: two materials that differ only in their specular response.
#
# Ks is the Phong specular colour and Ns the specular exponent. Neither has a PBR counterpart in the
# file, so these are exactly the inputs the conversion has to reason about, and the pair is chosen so
# that a mapping which ignored either one would be visible in the results:
#
#   MatShiny  Ks white       -> the ordinary dielectric response, Unreal's Specular 0.5
#             Ns 200         -> a tight highlight, so low roughness
#   MatDull   Ks 0.2 grey    -> a fifth of that response, Specular 0.1
#             Ns 4           -> a broad highlight, so roughness above the 0.5 default
#
# illum 2 declares the Phong model, which is what makes Ks meaningful at all.

newmtl MatShiny
Kd 0.800000 0.800000 0.800000
Ks 1.000000 1.000000 1.000000
Ns 200.000000
illum 2

newmtl MatDull
Kd 0.800000 0.800000 0.800000
Ks 0.200000 0.200000 0.200000
Ns 4.000000
illum 2
